  "derived_rule_id": "candidate:CAL-GOV-RULE-SINGLE-DECISION-CHECKPOINT",
  "derived_rule": "For every workflow instance w, its Workflow Decision Profile declares decision_mode none or single. Single mode must resolve exactly one Decision Checkpoint from the profile's allowed checkpoints using the most-specific applicable User Decision Preference or, when no preference exists, an explicit valid profile default. An invalid explicit preference blocks and never silently falls back. The checkpoint may present one closed Decision Bundle, but every decision retains its own Authority Boundary, owner, exact target, digest, effect, scope, outcome, and invalidation conditions. A later decision whose exact target does not yet exist belongs to a separate dependent workflow. Derived Refreshes require validation but no semantic decision.",
  "classification_consequence": "A normative-meaning change creates a Semantic Epoch. A canonical encoding change with preserved identity, Semantic Epoch, and normative meaning creates a Representation Revision. Regeneration from unchanged canonical input is a Derived Refresh. Therefore the current CTX08 v3 and v2-to-v3 lineage candidates are identified as open classification drift, not modified by this pack.",
  "workflow_dependency": {
